{"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Dealing With Customers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you deal with customers in a restaurant, you or the customer may ask for information or provide information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Generally when you ask for or provide information in a formal situation (customer to waiter), you use modals like <span class=\"italic\">can, could, will</span> and  <span class=\"italic\">would</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you are speaking to someone you know well (customer to customer), you are less formal and ask and answer questions more directly."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"More Formal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Less Formal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Waiter</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Are you sure you wouldn't like to look at the specials?</span><br/>   <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Customer</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">No thank you. I wouldn't.</span><br/><br/><br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Waiter</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">How would you like your filets cooked?</span><br/>  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Customer</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll have mine well done.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Miranda</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Don't you think that's extravagant, Edmund?</span><br/>   <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Edmund</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Nothing is too good for you, Miranda!</span> <br/><br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Miranda</span>:<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Are you sure, Edmund? A little bread is good with wine.</span><br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Edmund</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Oh fine. Let's have rolls.</span><br/> (this response is slightly impolite)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making Polite Requests and Responding to Polite Requests"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you make polite requests, you use modals like: <span class=\"italic\">can, could, will,</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you respond to requests, you can use future tenses like <span class=\"italic\">will, going to, the Present Simple</span> and <span class=\"italic\">the Present Continuous</span>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Make a Request\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Respond to a Request\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can I get sour cream with the potatoes?<span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Yes, <span class=\\\"strong\\\">we're serving</span> them with sour cream and chives.</span>  (Present Continuous)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'd also like the salad dressing on the side.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">That's not <span class=\\\"strong\\\">going to</span> be a problem. </span>  (Going to)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We'll have this Merlot with the steak.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">I'll</span> see if we have a bottle of that left.</span>  (Will)<br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Our wine delivery <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is</span> tomorrow.</span>  (Present Simple)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Would you like to keep the menus or can I take them?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm <span class=\\\"strong\\\">going to</span> have a look at the desserts, so please leave one.</span>  (Going to)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can I offer you a basket?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">No, thanks, we're not having rolls.</span>  (Present Continuous)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "well done"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "meat that is cooked thoroughly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll have my steak well done."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le02ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to order food."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sour cream"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a dairy product; fermented cream"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is there sour cream for the baked potatoes?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le02ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "on the side"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not on the plate or on top of the food"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Could I have my salad dressing on the side?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le02ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fillet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a premium cut of beef"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We'd both like fillet steaks, please."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le02ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "merlot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a type of red wine"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We'll have some merlot wine with our dinner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le02ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "roll"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small crust bread"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are small rolls this week to go with dinner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le02ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rare"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cooked to be pink or bloody inside"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I prefer my steak rare."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le02ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "salad dressing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a thick liquid to put on salad greens"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I have some salad dressing, please?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le02ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le02ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find an American restaurant online and look at the menu."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue asking a friend to come with you to the restaurant. (be polite and use modals)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use future tenses to say which dishes you are going to try. Ask what your friend is going to try on the menu."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the dialogue aloud with a partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles and read it again."}]}, {"type": "takeawa